cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: ".dotfiles"
abstract: >-
  Cross-platform, signed, local-first dotfiles for macOS, Linux, and WSL.
  Multi-shell parity across bash, zsh, fish, nushell and PowerShell, a
  chezmoi-managed configuration tree, the `dot` CLI control plane,
  wallpaper-driven terminal theming, and a release pipeline carrying SLSA
  provenance, sigstore signatures and an SBOM.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
    email: sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/dotfiles"
url: "https://doc.dotfiles.io/"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
version: 0.2.520
date-released: "2026-09-10"
keywords:
  - dotfiles
  - chezmoi
  - shell
  - zsh
  - fish
  - nushell
  - developer-environment
  - supply-chain-security
  - slsa
  - reproducible-configuration
